## Why This Is Asked

Tests understanding of stability and permutation-based sorting, ensuring candidates can separate data from its keys and reason about time/space trade-offs.

## Key Concepts

- Stable sort
- Permutations
- Time/space complexity
- Merge-based sorting on indices

## Code Example

```javascript
function stableSortIndicesByValue(A){
  const idx = Array.from({length: A.length}, (_, i) => i);
  function merge(left, right){
    const res = [];
    let i = 0, j = 0;
    while (i < left.length && j < right.length){
      if (A[left[i]] <= A[right[j]]) res.push(left[i++]);
      else res.push(right[j++]);
    }
    while (i < left.length) res.push(left[i++]);
    while (j < right.length) res.push(right[j++]);
    return res;
  }
  function sort(arr){
    if (arr.length <= 1) return arr;
    const m = Math.floor(arr.length / 2);
    const L = sort(arr.slice(0, m));
    const R = sort(arr.slice(m));
    return merge(L, R);
  }
  const P = sort(idx);
  return { P, sorted: P.map(i => A[i]) };
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Path auto-complete is a common editor feature; it probes practical data-structure trade-offs beyond textbooks.

## Key Concepts
- Trie with per-node children map
- Prefix search via traversal then DFS for completions
- Memory sharing of prefixes and separator handling

## Code Example
```javascript
class TrieNode {
  constructor() {
    this.next = new Map();
    this.isEnd = false;
  }
}
class PathTrie {
  constructor() { this.root = new TrieNode(); }
  insertPath(path) {
    let node = this.root;
    for (const ch of path) {
      if (!node.next.has(ch)) node.next.set(ch, new TrieNode());
      node = node.next.get(ch);
    }
    node.isEnd = true;
  }
  autocomplete(prefix, maxResults) {
    let node = this.root;
    for (const ch of prefix) {
      if (!node.next.has(ch)) return [];
      node = node.next.get(ch);
    }
    const results = [];
    const dfs = (cur, built) => {
      if (results.length >= maxResults) return;
      if (cur.isEnd) results.push(prefix + built);
      for (const [ch, child] of cur.next) dfs(child, built + ch);
    };
    dfs(node, "");
    return results;
  }
}
```

